  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 4 November 1922, in the Valley of the Kings, labourers engaged by the archaeologist Howard Carter uncovered a staircase carved into the rock. On 26 November, with his wealthy sponsor Lord Carnarvon beside him, Carter made a small hole in the sealed doorway and glimpsed the glittering gold of the boy king Tutankhamun. The spectacular find riveted the world."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        391.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Carnarvon sold exclusive rights to The Times, a monopoly that left competing reporters starved of news. Many resorted to speculation or sought outside commentators. In March 1923 the best-selling novelist Marie Corelli warned publicly that dire punishment awaited anyone who entered a sealed tomb. Within a fortnight, her words would seem uncanny."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        283.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        382.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "That month a mosquito bit Carnarvon. He nicked the bite with a razor while shaving, it turned septic, and blood poisoning led to pneumonia. He died in Cairo on 5 April 1923. Newspapers reported that the city's lights failed at that instant and that his dog in England howled and died. Yet blackouts were almost a daily occurrence in Cairo."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        176.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        275.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "No curse inscription was ever found in the tomb. In December 2002 a British Medical Journal study traced the fate of 44 Westerners in Egypt at the time. The 25 exposed to the tomb died at an average age of 70, versus 75 for the rest, a margin not statistically significant. The mortality figures lent the ominous rumour no credibility."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        167.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "Carnarvon's untimely demise had fuelled the tale, giving it impetus. Carter, the excavator who had unsealed the burial place, died in March 1939, aged 64, almost sixteen years after his patron. The legend had left him conspicuously unharmed."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1922年11月4日，在帝王谷，考古学家霍华德·卡特聘用的工人，发掘出了一段雕刻在岩石上面的阶梯。11月26日，在他那富有的赞助人卡纳冯勋爵的陪同下，卡特在封住的门道上开了一个小孔，并瞥见了少年国王图坦卡蒙闪闪发光的黄金。这一惊人的/壮观的发现，牢牢吸引了全世界的注意力。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "卡纳冯将独家的新闻报道权卖给了《泰晤士报》，这种垄断让相互竞争的其他记者严重缺少新闻。许多人（只能）诉诸于猜测，或者是找外界的评论员。1923年3月，畅销小说家玛丽·科雷利公开警告，极其严重的惩罚等待着任何进入封闭陵墓的人。两周之内，她的话就会显得诡异而又邪门。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        340.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "当月，一只蚊子叮了卡纳冯。他刮胡子时用剃刀划破了叮咬处，伤口感染化脓了，继而血液中毒又引发了肺炎。他于1923年4月5日在开罗去世。报纸报道称，就在那一瞬间，全城（开罗）的灯都熄灭了，而他在英国的狗也嚎叫着死去了。然而，停电在当时的开罗几乎是天天都有的事情。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        252.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        332.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "墓中从未发现过任何诅咒铭文。2002年12月，《英国医学杂志》的一项研究追溯了当时身在埃及的44名西方人的命运。其中曾接触这座陵墓的25人，平均死亡年龄为70岁，相比之下其余的人为75岁；这一差距在统计上并不显著。这些死亡数据让这则不祥的传言毫无可信度。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        183.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        243.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "卡纳冯的过早离世助长了这一传言，并为其推波助澜。卡特，这位启封了这处墓葬的发掘者，于1939年3月去世，终年64岁，距他的资助人去世已近十六年。这个传说偏偏让他毫发无损，这一点格外醒目。"
    }
  ],
